<title>USA: Texaco Texas lube oil plant idled by fire.</title>
<headline>Texaco Texas lube oil plant idled by fire.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc said a Galena Park, Texas lube oil blending and packaging plant near Houston was idled by a small fire in a storage room early Thursday.</p>
<p>About six to 10 workers were evacuated when the fire was discovered at about 0530 CST, and local firefighters extinguished the flames. Operations at the facility will be restarted this afternoon, a Texaco spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>One firefighter was injured hooking up a hose to battle the flames, she said. The facility employs 121 workers.</p>
</text>
